# Thin page shells

`components/pages/*` are CRM slug shells only — not feature homes.

## Required

1. Page files re-export or render one domain root (like [`components/pages/AccessControl.tsx`](components/pages/AccessControl.tsx) → `components/access-control/`).
2. Put `useState`, upload/sync handlers, modals, and list widgets in `components/<domain>/` (or existing sibling folders: `tour-design/`, `gallery/`, `products/`, …).
3. Do **not** add heavy handlers or new multi-hundred-line JSX to a page file when extending a feature — extract first.

## Soft target

- New or refactored page shells: preferably under ~50 lines.
- If a page file exceeds ~400 lines, split into the domain folder before adding features.

## Canonical example

Access Control: thin `pages/AccessControl.tsx` + widgets under `components/access-control/`.
